commit a2b192295d7046bafc18d54973436bb3faa659d7
Author: Andreas Gruenbacher <andreas.gruenbacher@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri May 15 01:12:04 2026 +0200

    Absolute in-tree symlink target resolved relative to symlink parent
    
    When resolving an absolute symlink that points back into patch's working
    directory, patch resolved the remainder of the symlink relative to the
    directory containing the symlink rather than the working directory.  With
    symlinks in subdirectories, this can lead to patching the wrong file.
    * src/safe.c (struct symlink): Store the cached_dirfd a symlink resolves to.
    (cwd): Turn into a global variable that can be accessed from read-symlink().
    (read_symlink): Pass the current cached_dirfd and return the cached_dirfd the
    symlink needs to be resolved in.
    (traverse_next): Continue traversal in the directory returned by
    read_symlink().
    * tests/symlinks: Add absolute symlink test case.
    
    This closes bug #68311:
    https://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/?68311

